1
00:05:35,625 --> 00:05:41,625
One ring to rule them all.

2
00:11:11,250 --> 00:11:17,250
The Lord of the Rings: The Fellowship of the Ring is a adventure,
fantasy, action film directed by Peter Jackson.

3
00:16:46,875 --> 00:16:52,875
Young hobbit Frodo Baggins, after inheriting a mysterious ring from his uncle Bilbo, must leave
his home in order to keep it from falling into the hands of its evil creator.

4
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:28,500
Along the way, a fellowship is formed to protect the ringbearer and make
sure that the ring arrives at its final destination: Mt.

5
00:27:58,125 --> 00:28:04,125
Doom, the only place where it can be destroyed.

6
00:33:33,750 --> 00:33:39,750
Frodo, played by Elijah Wood.

7
00:39:09,375 --> 00:39:15,375
Gandalf, played by Ian McKellen.

8
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:51,000
Aragorn, played by Viggo Mortensen.

9
00:50:20,625 --> 00:50:26,625
Sam, played by Sean Astin.

10
00:55:56,250 --> 00:56:02,250
Bilbo, played by Ian Holm.

11
01:01:31,875 --> 01:01:37,875
Arwen, played by Liv Tyler.

12
01:07:07,500 --> 01:07:13,500
The Lord of the Rings: The Fellowship of the Ring is a 2001 epic high fantasy adventure film
directed by Peter Jackson from a screenplay by Fran Walsh, Philippa Boyens, and Jackson.

13
01:12:43,125 --> 01:12:49,125
It is based on J.

14
01:18:18,750 --> 01:18:24,750
Tolkien's 1954 The Fellowship of the Ring, the first
volume of the novel The Lord of the Rings.

15
01:23:54,375 --> 01:24:00,375
The film is the first instalment in The Lord of the Rings trilogy.

16
01:29:30,000 --> 01:29:36,000
It features an ensemble cast including Elijah Wood, Ian McKellen, Liv Tyler, Viggo Mortensen, Sean Astin, Cate Blanchett, John
Rhys-Davies, Billy Boyd, Dominic Monaghan, Orlando Bloom, Christopher Lee, Hugo Weaving, Sean Bean, Ian Holm, and Andy Serkis.

17
01:35:05,625 --> 01:35:11,625
Set in Middle-earth, the story tells of the Dark Lord Sauron, who seeks the
One Ring, which contains part of his might, to return to power.

18
01:40:41,250 --> 01:40:47,250
The Ring has found its way to the young hobbit Frodo Baggins.

19
01:46:16,875 --> 01:46:22,875
The fate of Middle-earth hangs in the balance as Frodo and eight companions (who form the eponymous Fellowship of the Ring)
begin their perilous journey to Mount Doom in the land of Mordor, the only place where the Ring can be destroyed.

20
01:51:52,500 --> 01:51:58,500
The Fellowship of the Ring was financed and distributed by American studio New Line Cinema, but filmed and edited
entirely in Jackson's native New Zealand, concurrently with the other two parts of the trilogy.

21
01:57:28,125 --> 01:57:34,125
It premiered on 10 December 2001 at the Odeon Leicester Square in London and was released
on 19 December in the United States and on 20 December in New Zealand.

22
02:03:03,750 --> 02:03:09,750
The film was acclaimed by critics and audiences, who considered it a landmark in filmmaking and an achievement in the fantasy film genre, with
praise for the visual effects, performances, direction, screenplay, musical score, and faithfulness to the source material.

23
02:08:39,375 --> 02:08:45,375
It grossed $868 million worldwide during its original theatrical run, making it the second-highest-grossing
film of 2001 and the fifth-highest-grossing film of all time at the time of its release.

24
02:14:15,000 --> 02:14:21,000
Following subsequent reissues, it has grossed $896 million.

25
02:19:50,625 --> 02:19:56,625
Like its successors, The Fellowship of the Ring is widely recognised as
one of the greatest and most influential films ever made.

26
02:25:26,250 --> 02:25:32,250
The film received numerous accolades; at the 74th Academy Awards, it was nominated for thirteen awards, including Best
Picture, winning for Best Cinematography, Best Makeup, Best Original Score, and Best Visual Effects.

27
02:31:01,875 --> 02:31:07,875
In 2007, the American Film Institute named it one of the 100 greatest American films in history, being both
the most recent film and the only film released in the 21st century to make it to the list.

28
02:36:37,500 --> 02:36:43,500
In 2021, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress for being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

29
02:42:13,125 --> 02:42:19,125
Two sequels, The Two Towers and The Return of the King,
followed in 2002 and 2003, respectively.

30
02:47:48,750 --> 02:47:54,750
The film explores themes of based on novel or
book, elves, dwarf, magic, obsession.

31
02:53:24,375 --> 02:53:30,375
The tone is intense.
